# Cloudflare Pages custom headers — see https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# This is the frontend-hardening layer described in docs/SECURITY.md: it protects
# users of the site itself (clickjacking, MIME-sniffing, a compromised third-party
# script trying to exfiltrate data) — it has no effect on the contracts, which is
# where mint/burn/pause/blacklist are actually gated. See the in-app Security
# Center (/tools/security) for that side of things.
#
# NOTE ON THE CSP BELOW: it's intentionally permissive on connect-src/img-src/frame-src
# because a wallet app (ConnectKit + WalletConnect) legitimately talks to a wide, sometimes-
# changing set of relay/verify/RPC/wallet-deeplink origins. Tightening those further is
# easy to get wrong and break "Connect Wallet" silently — if you narrow them, check the
# browser console for CSP violation reports on every wallet flow (connect, sign, switch
# network) before shipping, ideally with `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only` first.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; frame-src https:; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https:; font-src 'self' https: data:; img-src 'self' https: data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https: wss:; worker-src 'self' blob:; upgrade-insecure-requests
